{
  "scenario": "A record label, Northwind Records, licenses an album and its four tracks. Its catalogue-wide Set policy prohibits modifying the recordings, with deleting modified copies as the remedy; an Offer inherits from it and lets anyone stream the album for a per-stream fee; and an Agreement with the streaming service Tunely inherits from the offer, permitting it to stream and play the album in the EU or the UK until the end of 2027, with duties to pay, to attribute the artist and to report usage monthly, and a prohibition on commercialising it. ODRL's actions, left operands and operators are nodes keyed by their ODRL IRIs; the companies and their IRIs are fictional.",
